<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Organizations on Layer5 Documentation</title><link>/pr-preview/pr-1329/cloud/guides/organizations/</link><description>Recent content in Organizations on Layer5 Documentation</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en</language><atom:link href="/pr-preview/pr-1329/cloud/guides/organizations/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Organization Configuration Scenarios</title><link>/pr-preview/pr-1329/cloud/guides/organizations/configuration-scenarios/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>/pr-preview/pr-1329/cloud/guides/organizations/configuration-scenarios/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Every organization in Layer5 Cloud is configured by two choices: &lt;strong&gt;where your users sign in&lt;/strong&gt; (the front door) and &lt;strong&gt;whose identity provider authenticates them&lt;/strong&gt;. The combinations form five named scenarios. This guide helps you pick one and then walks through the settings that implement it, including who is allowed to change each setting.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For the mechanics behind the choices, see &lt;a href="/pr-preview/pr-1329/cloud/guides/self-hosted/white-labeling/"&gt;White-labeling&lt;/a&gt; (themes, logos, custom domains) and &lt;a href="/pr-preview/pr-1329/cloud/guides/self-hosted/planning/identity-services/"&gt;Identity Services&lt;/a&gt; (bring-your-own-credentials and authentication boundaries).&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Manage Teams</title><link>/pr-preview/pr-1329/cloud/guides/organizations/managing-teams/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>/pr-preview/pr-1329/cloud/guides/organizations/managing-teams/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;This guide covers the administrator tasks for teams. For what a team is and how it grants access, read the &lt;a href="/pr-preview/pr-1329/cloud/concepts/identity-and-security/teams/"&gt;Teams concept&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;














