&lt;h2 id="create-a-team" class="heading-link"&gt;
 Create a team
 &lt;a href="#create-a-team" class="heading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink to this heading"&gt;🔗&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Needs:&lt;/strong&gt; the Create Team permission in your current organization.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Recognize Members with Badges</title><link>/pr-preview/pr-1329/cloud/guides/organizations/assigning-user-badges/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>/pr-preview/pr-1329/cloud/guides/organizations/assigning-user-badges/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;A &lt;strong&gt;recognition&lt;/strong&gt; is a badge that an organization defines and awards to its members. Recognitions mark milestones such as completing training, contributing to a project, or reaching a team goal. An awarded badge appears on the recipient&amp;rsquo;s public profile, where the recipient can share it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Two kinds of badges exist, and they come from different places:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Organization recognitions&lt;/strong&gt; are created and awarded by an organization&amp;rsquo;s administrators. This guide covers them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Layer5 community badges&lt;/strong&gt; belong to the Layer5 community recognition program. Browse them in the &lt;a href="https://badges.layer5.io"&gt;Badge Gallery&lt;/a&gt; and read how they are earned in the &lt;a href="https://layer5.io/community/handbook/recognition"&gt;Recognition section of the Layer5 Community Handbook&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2 id="who-can-do-what" class="heading-link"&gt;
 Who can do what
 &lt;a href="#who-can-do-what" class="heading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink to this heading"&gt;🔗&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
 &lt;thead&gt;
 &lt;tr&gt;
 &lt;th&gt;Task&lt;/th&gt;
 &lt;th&gt;What it needs&lt;/th&gt;
 &lt;/tr&gt;
 &lt;/thead&gt;
 &lt;tbody&gt;
 &lt;tr&gt;
 &lt;td&gt;Create, edit, or delete a recognition&lt;/td&gt;
 &lt;td&gt;The &lt;strong&gt;Manage Recognitions&lt;/strong&gt; permission in the organization that owns the recognition. Organization Admin, Provider Admin, and Academy Admin hold it by default. The &lt;strong&gt;Manage Recognitions&lt;/strong&gt; control on the Organizations page is enabled for holders of &lt;strong&gt;Edit Organization&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/td&gt;
 &lt;/tr&gt;
 &lt;tr&gt;
 &lt;td&gt;Award a recognition to a member&lt;/td&gt;
 &lt;td&gt;The permission to update that member&amp;rsquo;s profile, held in an organization you share with the member.&lt;/td&gt;
 &lt;/tr&gt;
 &lt;tr&gt;
 &lt;td&gt;View a badge&lt;/td&gt;
 &lt;td&gt;Anyone who can open the recipient&amp;rsquo;s public profile.&lt;/td&gt;
 &lt;/tr&gt;
 &lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Two limits apply to every award:&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>